# Never ship to Posit Connect.
#
# ⚠️ WILDCARDS DO NOT WORK HERE. rsconnect matches .rscignore entries as EXACT file or directory
# names — no globs, no patterns. The lines below used to read `data/*.bak-*` and `*.bak-*`, which
# matched nothing at all, and `rsconnect::writeManifest(appDir = ".")` duly swept 40 MB of database
# snapshots, .claude/, and scratch notes into the deployment. (Caught 2026-07-12.)
#
# Because a wildcard cannot express "every .bak-* that will ever exist", DO NOT regenerate the
# manifest with a bare appDir. Pass an explicit file list:
#
#     files <- <the 34 files that actually constitute the app>
#     rsconnect::writeManifest(appDir = ".", appFiles = files)
#
# `make check` (root) asserts the manifest contains no .bak/scratch files and that every checksum
# in it matches the file on disk.

rsconnect/
.claude/
prompts/
